### 1. Get all students (PostgreSQL)
GET http://localhost:5239/api/students?db=postgres

### 2. Get all students (SQL Server)
GET http://localhost:5239/api/students?db=sqlserver

### 3. Create student - Success (PostgreSQL)
POST http://localhost:5239/api/students?db=postgres
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentNumber": "40110001",
  "firstName": "Mehdi",
  "lastName": "Ahmadi",
  "isMale": true,
  "grade": 18.5,
  "dateOfBirth": "2005-05-15T00:00:00",
  "leftUnitsCount": 12
}

### 4. Create student - Success (SQL Server)
POST http://localhost:5239/api/students?db=sqlserver
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentNumber": "40110002",
  "firstName": "Sara",
  "lastName": "Rezaei",
  "isMale": false,
  "grade": 19.25,
  "dateOfBirth": "2004-03-20T00:00:00",
  "leftUnitsCount": 10
}

### 5. Create - Duplicate Student Number (Expects 409 Conflict)
POST http://localhost:5239/api/students?db=postgres
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentNumber": "40110001",
  "firstName": "Mehdi",
  "lastName": "Duplicate",
  "isMale": true,
  "grade": 15.0,
  "dateOfBirth": "2005-05-15T00:00:00",
  "leftUnitsCount": 5
}

### 6. Create - Invalid Student Number Length (Expects 400)
POST http://localhost:5239/api/students?db=postgres
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentNumber": "123",
  "firstName": "Ali",
  "lastName": "Test",
  "isMale": true,
  "grade": 17.0,
  "dateOfBirth": "2005-01-01T00:00:00",
  "leftUnitsCount": 10
}

### 7. Create - First Name > 20 chars (Expects 400)
POST http://localhost:5239/api/students?db=postgres
Content-Type: application/json

